ave more  room for taste buds  people with more than 30 taste buds in  an  area the size of a hole punch belong to  an  elite group known as super tasters  every flavor bitter or sweet might send  you into sensory overload  yeah of course that's assuming you can  get actual  food into your body since you wouldn't  be able to close your mouth  you wouldn't be able to chew instead you  would have to have your food  liquefied and syringed onto the back of  your tongue  or take your nutrients through an iv  and with so many papillae on your tongue  your mouth might become a breeding  ground for bacteria  these raised grooves already collect  bits of food and residue from  every meal so each bite of protein-rich  foods like  milk or cheese could live in your mouth  long past their expiration date your  morning breath would last  all day long  now if the thought of all these live  bacteria crawling around inside your  mouth  doesn't keep you up at night maybe the  sleep apnea will  after all this colossal muscle will get  in the way of your breathing causing you  to snore  or wake up throughout the night like  your heart  your tongue works during your sleep  while you rest your tongue helps you  swallow the excess fluids building in  your mouth  if you couldn't find a way to restrain  your tongue  you might choke on your own saliva  the tongue stands as the last defender  against  harmful substances entering your body  your body has a gag reflex that  triggers when the area on the back of  your tongue contracts but  with a tongue this huge you may not be  able to force out anything other than a  groan and  since your mouth would never be closed  you might be drooling everywhere your  teeth could become misaligned and  protrude outward and  your tongue would become dry and maybe  even infected  your mouth cavity can't hold a tongue  this long  and the only way you could resume an  everyday life would be through surgery  but if you had the extra room in your  head  maybe yo